nodecode-taint-sentry is a rewrite of YAN-XBT's YAN-XBT/hermes-sentry:

  https://github.com/YAN-XBT/hermes-sentry
  commit 5f74fe9c923f228a2b6e6aa95d362b71b94bfc20
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 YAN-XBT (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provenance classification (which tools and which calls produce
third-party content), the text hygiene (invisible characters removed, the
instruction signatures named), the per-session taint marks with a TTL and file
artifacts, the ten rules of the policy with their taint/always switch and their
allow_hosts and allow_paths escapes, the untrusted envelope with its notes, and
the two read-only tools. The four Hermes hooks became one Nodecode hook:
transform_tool_result and pre_tool_call are the before and after halves of the
:TOOL point, and subagent_start is the same session's marks read by the
subagent's calls.

Left out, and why: the SQLite receipts ledger, the `hermes taint-sentry` CLI
with its dry-run tester and its clear-request marker file, the desktop pane and
the dashboard's plugin API and rule-editing route, and the debug trace rows.
None of them is a decision -- they are where the decisions are read back; the
cell answers the same questions from a ring of the session's newest receipts,
a slash command, and (help :taint-sentry). The pre_llm_call banner is carried
by the envelope and the manual instead of a standing prompt block, because
Nodecode has no prompt-construction point a cell may hook. The decoding of
obfuscated payloads (`powershell -enc <base64>`) that the original re-judges as
its own call is not carried: the pattern rules read the command as written.
